  {
    "key": "Stylized Fantasy Turtle",
    "value": [
      {
        "templateID": "5",
        "data": {
          "images": [],
          "texts": [
            "I created this asset for a game called Turtle Town, but it did not get used due to team dysfunction.\r\n\r\nI sculpted and retopologized the turtle model in ZBrush, painted the textures in Substance Painter, and rigged it in Maya LT.\r\n\r\nThe screenshots you see are in Unity engine with orthographic projection, as was the intended display format for the game project.\r\n\r\nThe turtle is rendered using a stylized shader which gives an outline effect as well as quantized lighting bands. The shader was part of my art direction, but I did not code it."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "templateID": "1",
        "data": {
          "images": [
            "/projects/Stylized Fantasy Turtle/project-details/1/turtle-rig.png"
          ],
          "texts": []
        }
      },
      {
        "templateID": "5",
        "data": {
          "images": [],
          "texts": [
            "The game's focus was to build a base on the back of a giant, living turtle. On the back of the turtle are stylized trees and monolithic rocks that jut from its shell.\r\n\r\nThe turtle is rigged to animate 3 tiers of progress for the player. Each town hall upgrade clears rocks and trees from the back of the turtle, openning up new areas for the player to expand their city:"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "templateID": "1",
        "data": {
          "images": [
